AVL Tree

Description
This program implements a self-balancing Binary Search Tree known as an AVL Tree. It maintains balance by tracking the height and balance factor of each node upon insertion. If an insertion causes any node's balance factor to fall outside the range of -1 to 1, the tree automatically rebalances itself using Left, Right, Left-Right, or Right-Left rotations. The program inserts six elements and prints the Preorder traversal, Inorder traversal, and the final height of the tree (using 0-based height indexing where a leaf node has a height of 0).

Time and Space Complexity
Insertion: O(log n) time in both average and worst cases because the tree remains balanced.
Rotations and Height Updates: O(1) time per operation.
Preorder and Inorder Traversals: O(n) time to visit all n nodes in the tree.
Space Complexity: O(n) auxiliary space to store the nodes, and O(log n) recursion stack space during insertion and traversal.

Sample Output
Preorder Traversal: 30 20 10 25 40 50
Inorder Traversal: 10 20 25 30 40 50
Height of AVL Tree: 2
